1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
"Company Worker - Ukai Tsuneo (47)"

2
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
He spoke it!

3
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
"Role of Sakamoto Ryoma, Sakuraba Reiichi"

4
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:06,140
"Conan Special Drama Kudo Shinichi's
Kyoto Shinsengumi Murder Case"

5
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,720
You rebel ronin who defy the Shogunate!
"Osaka's High School Detective - Hattori Heiji"

6
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:33,160
This Shinsengumi, Okita Soji,
will be your opponent.

7
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,240
En garde.

8
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,200
This isn’t over!

9
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:58,920
-Cut! Cut!
-You there!

10
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,960
How many times do I have to tell you?

11
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:03,840
When you're stabbed, just die
already! Just drop dead!

12
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:07,560
This Mori Kogoro will not fall so easily!
"Private Detective - Mori Kogoro"

13
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:11,960
Fool! You're just a mere extra!

14
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:13,930
Alright! One more time!
"Heiji's Childhood Friend Toyama Kazuha"

15
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:16,920
-One more time, please!
-No, no! This is my spotlight.

16
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,560
Look, it's also written right here.

17
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:23,900
You are the protagonist!,
Ryoma's Holiday.

18
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,240
That's a common dream to write down.

19
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:30,720
Fool! You samurai boy!

20
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,400
What is life without a dream?!

21
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,680
It's still too early to give up.
I'll appeal directly to the Director!

22
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:41,520
Director! Please give me a
chance! I'll do my best...

23
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,180
Ran, it's been ages!

24
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:46,720
Actually, when Heiji was in
the middle of a kendo contest...

25
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:49,120
...he had been scouted
for a historical film.

26
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,240
So we're now in Kyoto
shooting it, but...

27
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,500
"Why don't you come see
the shoot?"

28
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:56,780
Sounds fun!

29
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,280
Shinichi, do you want
to go together?

30
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,200
We can zoom over there by plane.

31
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:03,760
That’s dangerous!
I'm not interested in movies.

32
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:07,800
Actually you're just jealous about
Hattori's achievements, right?

33
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,480
Fool! No way!

34
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:15,720
Kudo-sempai! Kyaa!

35
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:20,160
-How was your last case?
-That was just an easy trick.

36
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:23,960
-Please give me your autograph!
-Please shake my hand!

37
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:27,840
-Another time.
-Kyaa! So cool!

38
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:35,000
Ehh... Even if you're not
interested in movies...

39
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:37,880
...you are interested in the junior girls.

40
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,880
What are you saying?

41
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,440
You turn down an invitation
from your childhood friend...

42
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:46,440
But you'll be giving those
junior girls your autograph?

43
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,600
Ah, alright already. I understand.

44
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,160
-Excuse me!
- I'll go.

45
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,760
It's fine if I go, right?

46
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,500
"High School Student Detective -
Kudo Shinichi"

47
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:12,080
My name is Kudo Shinichi.

48
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:15,540
<i>I'm a famous high school
student detective.</i>

49
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:20,880
<i>But one day when I went with my
childhood friend Ran to an amusement park,</i>

50
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:25,040
<i>I witnessed a scene of some men in
black involved in some suspicious deal.</i>

51
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:30,280
<i>And then one of those men made me
 take a poison known as Apoptoxin 4869.</i>

52
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:34,320
<i>When I woke up,
my body had shrunken.</i>

53
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:37,880
<i>If they knew that
Kudo Shinichi was still alive...</i>

54
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,280
<i>...the Black Organization could bring
harm to people around me.</i>

55
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,160
Naming myself Edogawa Conan...

56
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:45,300
I solved cases while looking for
information on those men.

57
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:50,620
But this story was from long
before I became Edogawa Conan.

58
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:58,360
"Conan Special Drama Kudo Shinichi's
Kyoto Shinsengumi Murder Case"

59
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:03,560
"LUNA Airlines/Flight 576"

60
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:18,840
What is it?
I just heard a scream.

61
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,000
There...

62
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,860
This is...

63
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,880
He's dead.

64
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:40,000
That Shinichi...
Where did he go?

65
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,840
-I'm Sato of the MPD.
-I'm Takagi of the same.

66
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,800
No one has touched
the body, right?

67
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:49,920
Well, strange young man earlier.

68
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,680
-A strange young man?
-Yes.

69
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:54,440
-Excuse us.
-I'm sorry.

70
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,330
The cause of death was probably...

71
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,460
...suffocation due to a 
cervical spinal cord injury.

72
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,100
The weapon was the sharpened
point of a dull-edged tool.

73
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,320
Something like an ice pick.

74
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:09,760
When a human is struck here,
in the respiratory center of the medulla...

75
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:12,500
The respiratory neurons
pathways become impaired...

76
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:16,040
...causing the victim to be unable to
breathe nor speak leading to death.

77
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:21,440
But before the victim was struck,
he was made to inhale chemicals...

78
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:24,040
...causing him to fall into a coma first.

79
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,400
But don't worry.

80
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:31,240
The criminal is still here in
this huge clump of iron.

81
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,600
Hey! Who are you?!

82
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:37,180
<i>Yes. That was the first page.</i>

83
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,520
Kudo Shinichi.

84
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:41,760
Detective.

85
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:47,880
<i>This was the first case of high school
student detective, Kudo Shinichi.</i>

86
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:52,780
"The Closed-room Murder
at 10,000 meters"

87
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:57,920
The victim is Otaka Kazuhiro, 29.
A professional photographer.

88
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:58,900
About half a year ago...

89
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:02,640
...I read a newspaper article about
him winning the Press Photo Award.

90
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:06,760
By the way, his passport was
inside his inner vest pocket.

91
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:10,240
It was important to him, and
that may be why he put it in there.

92
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:14,120
- Sorry, but this is police work!
- Hey, get out!

93
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,180
Children should stay out of this!

94
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:18,680
Ah, since we would like to take
some photos of the crime scene...

95
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:20,000
...could we borrow
a camera from you?

96
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,960
I took a photo of it already.

97
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,160
Shinichi?

98
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:26,220
Based upon the condition of postmortem
lividity and the rigidity of his jaw...

99
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:28,700
...I believe that 1 to 2 hours
have passed since his death.

100
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:29,840
I don’t know where
you heard all these, but...

101
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:32,320
There are 3 things bothering me.

102
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:37,860
First is that while there are bloodstains on
the wall where the corpse was resting…

103
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:41,980
But there aren't any clinging
to his clothes at all.

104
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:46,200
Second is that there is another wound
to the lower left of the mortal wound.

105
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:49,140
A mark as if he had been scratched
with the edge of something.

106
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:54,720
Thirdly is that the insides of his pants
pockets are soaked for some reason.

107
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,980
Even if he had poked his wet hands into
them, they wouldn't have gotten that wet.

108
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:00,440
-Ouch!
-Stop this!

109
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:04,480
-There's no reason to hit me.
-I told you this is police work!

110
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:08,600
Um, in order to check for witnesses
of any suspicious people...

111
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:11,920
-Could you please gather the passengers?
-There's no need for that.

112
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,460
There are just 4 suspects.

113
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:16,620
Wait!

114
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:20,060
Why are you saying such bossy things 
for! You're just a high school student!

115
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:22,820
Why would you say that
there are only 4 of them?

116
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:27,940
My seat was at the far back.

117
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:30,220
People going to the restrooms
would have had to go pass me...

118
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,500
...and there were
no passengers behind me.

119
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:35,440
Of those who did go to the restroom
around the estimated time of death...

120
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:38,260
...aside from the victim,
there were just 4 people.

121
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,060
By checking their faces,
I would recognize them instantly.

122
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:44,240
Don't tell me you were
awake all night?

123
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:48,260
Well, I guess.
I just couldn't sleep that easily.

124
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,800
Fool!

125
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:54,180
Seeing that sleeping face of yours...

126
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,580
There was no way
I could just calmly go to sleep.

127
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,700
-You said something?
-Ah, nothing.

128
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:02,580
Well, since you're willing
to go that far...

129
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:05,320
Let's see if you know
who those 4 people are.

130
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,780
Sure.

131
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:12,280
Let's see...
The 4 people are...

132
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:13,860
Ah...

133
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:16,980
This woman here and
the woman next to her...

134
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:20,020
The man across from
them in the aisle seat...

135
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:23,140
And this foreigner in
the seat in front of them.

136
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:27,260
Otaka's seat was...right here, correct?

137
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:30,340
They were all sitting in proximity
to the victim, weren't they?

138
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:32,500
"Victim"?
What do you mean by that?

139
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,000
Excuse me.

140
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:38,080
For now, the four of you
please come to rear restrooms.

141
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,120
We'll discuss the circumstances there.

142
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:48,020
No... Otaka! Otaka!!

143
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,880
Cannot be...

144
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:55,800
-No way...
-Excuse me, you are?

145
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:59,160
Ah... Along with these two women,
we're photographers just like Otaka.

146
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:01,600
Say, do I have the right
to hear what happened?

147
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:04,500
Well, since you are
the victim’s associates.

148
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:11,980
You were sitting near the victim, Otaka,
but what is your connection to him?

149
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:14,660
I had no relation to him.

150
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:17,080
I'm just an ordinary salaryman
off on a business trip.

151
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:22,580
I and Saginuma were traveling
along with Otaka as friends.

152
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:28,000
Tsugumi was... Otaka's girlfriend.

153
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,800
And the one other person is a foreigner.

154
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:34,480
-Takagi, how's your English?
-Ah, I can speak a little.

155
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:39,360
-Hmmm, let's see...
-(What was your relationship to the victim?)

156
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:43,700
(It was my first time to see him.
I just came to Japan to buy artwork.)

157
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,340
(Thanks!)

158
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,440
He said that he wasn't
an acquaintance of Otaka's...

159
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:50,820
...and only came to Japan
to buy artwork.

160
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,460
Thank you!

161
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:59,080
Ah! Could it be...

162
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:03,220
Once we get there, these negatives
will fetch a high price...

163
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,360
...and we can vacation all we want!

164
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:07,260
You should be happy having
such a nice boyfriend, right!

165
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:10,720
-Wait Otaka, be quiet.
-Eh?

166
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:13,060
Could you be quiet?

167
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:17,620
-Everyone is trying to sleep.
-Ah, my bad.

168
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:21,040
I'll be careful next time!

169
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:24,840
Otaka! Stop it already!

170
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:28,580
Yes, yes. I understand.

171
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:32,400
Such a scary woman.
Right, Saginuma?

172
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,920
What a boring guy, the bastard.

173
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,420
Guess I'll take a nap, too.

174
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:45,600
Maybe he was killed
because of those negatives...

175
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,820
But no negatives were found
on Otaka's corpse.

176
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:52,340
Eh? He should have been keeping
them in his inner vest pocket.

177
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:55,680
I see. I'm sure the criminal
took them away.

178
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:58,260
Firstly, would each of the 4 of you...

179
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:01,760
...tell me what happened
when you went to the restroom?

180
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:06,680
When I returned from the restroom...

181
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,880
Otaka was in his seat.

182
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:12,620
I remembered feeling a little ill,
so I called the stewardess.

183
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:15,280
-Can I help you?
-I'm sorry.

184
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,080
Do you have any medicine
to stop motion sickness?

185
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,440
Yes. Please wait just a moment.

186
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:23,700
I also saw the male victim from
the opposite aisle over there.

187
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:27,800
Why were you in the opposite aisle?

188
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:30,240
I was just wandering around
since I was restless.

189
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:31,700
Though I had been
sleeping soundly...

190
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:35,140
...because of a noisy passenger,
I was woken up.

191
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:39,480
It’s that man. It was when
Tsugumi was asking for medicine...

192
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,040
...that I saw the male victim.

193
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:44,500
I went to the restroom
right after that.

194
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:50,100
I was woken up when the
stewardess brought the medicine...

195
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:53,080
But at that time
Otaka wasn't there any longer.

196
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:55,720
Did you take the motion
sickness medicine I gave you?

197
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:57,140
Yeah...

198
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:58,760
That's strange...

199
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:03,200
I’ve given some to Saginuma, too,
but it seems to work on him.

200
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,420
In that case,
why don't we switch seats?

201
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,520
If you're next to a window,
maybe that'll change your mood.

202
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:09,080
Yes, alright.

203
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,980
Thanks.

204
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,440
Excuse me.
The medicine is for her.

205
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:23,320
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

206
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,540
-Here.
-Thank you.

207
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:31,940
Oh. Where's Otaka?

208
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:35,540
Ah...Looks like he went somewhere.

209
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,940
To the restroom? Otaka...
I then went to the restroom.

210
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,760
Then it can be said Otaka left
his seat to go to the restroom...

211
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:47,900
...after Tsugumi asked for the medicine
but before it was brought to her, right?

212
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:51,720
Then after that, Chizuru you said
you went to the restroom...

213
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,120
I didn't kill him!

214
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:57,520
That said, when I went to
the restroom, Otaka was still alive!

215
00:12:57,700 --> 00:13:01,120
When I asked if he was okay and
knocked, he knocked back!

216
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,780
You knew exactly which restroom
he entered, didn't you?

217
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:08,900
Eh?

218
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:13,160
Because the locks to all
the other restrooms were open.

219
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:18,000
Then, the last person...

220
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,960
(When were you in the bathroom?)

221
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:23,720
(I don't remember what time it was.)

222
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:27,000
He says he doesn't remember
when he went in.

223
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:29,900
What's the matter?

224
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:34,280
Well...the smell of
his cologne is so strong.

225
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:38,020
And now we've heard the stories of
everyone who went to the restroom, but...

226
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:40,900
Just a moment please.

227
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:45,080
There was one other person
who left their seat.

228
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,860
This man.

229
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,520
Huh?!

230
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,960
I was asleep the entire time!

231
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:56,840
Your seat was directly behind
the murdered Otaka, right?

232
00:13:57,320 --> 00:14:01,300
When Otaka was sleeping,
there was no one in that seat.

233
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:04,720
In other words,
you must have left your seat!

234
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:06,880
Stop bullshittting me!

235
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:09,900
Didn’t he say that
the 4 of you left your seats?

236
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:13,620
-Right?
-Eh? Ah, well...

237
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:17,060
Hey! Be certain!

238
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:20,920
Thing is...

239
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:24,500
I have a feeling I was
distracted for a moment...

240
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:28,860
-Eh?!
-Well, it was you...

241
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,120
Anyhow, rather than listening
to our testimonies...

242
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,100
...wouldn’t it be faster to find either
the negatives or the murder weapon?

243
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,340
That's certainly true.

244
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:39,720
Well then, let’s do a body check on
all of you and a check of your luggage.

245
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:42,700
-Are you okay with that?
-Huh? Me, too?

246
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:45,280
Would that inconvenience
you somehow?

247
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:50,740
Let's see. Next is Tsugumi.

248
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:53,740
In here we have a passport, a wallet...

249
00:14:53,880 --> 00:14:56,860
...and a sewing set with scissors...

250
00:14:56,980 --> 00:15:00,040
...but it would be impossible
to kill someone with these.

251
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,840
Have you checked
the contents of the pen?

252
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:02,780
Yes?

253
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:05,440
It would be possible to hide the deadly
weapon as part of its core section.

254
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:06,480
Core?

255
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:09,200
Core… the core!
I'll check the core now.

256
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:12,540
Ah look, the core is in good order.

257
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:16,120
Let's see, next is...

258
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:18,740
...oh, it’s Mr. Edward.

259
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:23,920
This is a checkbook from
the American National Bank...

260
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:28,080
Ah, you...

261
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:31,860
(What were you going
to use this checkbook for?)

262
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,520
(I brought it to buy pieces
at a Japanese auction.)

263
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:37,900
(Ah, collecting artwork
is a hobby of mine.)

264
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:42,320
(Unfortunately, it was all junk
and a waste of time.)

265
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:46,080
He says it was in order to purchase
artwork but that he didn't get to use it.

266
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:52,140
(I can tell you have a great sense
of art from that beautiful watch.)

267
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,260
-(Can I take a look?)
-(Sure.)

268
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:01,920
<i>Though the smell of his cologne
was quite strong around his neck...</i>

269
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:04,360
<i>...I couldn't smell anything
from his wrist.</i>

270
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:07,000
<i>Didn't he put any on his wrist?</i>

271
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,980
(Thanks.)

272
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:13,780
Then, next is...
Saginuma, right?

273
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:18,020
Here you are.
Knock yourself out.

274
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:22,540
Ah, um, this, too...
Let's see...

275
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,780
You seem to have a lot of medicine
to prevent motion sickness.

276
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,660
I'm weak when it comes
to vehicles, you see.

277
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,980
I’ve gotten them from
Tsugumi and Chizuro, right?

278
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,500
Yeah.

279
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,580
These are...negatives, aren't they?

280
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:36,640
What about them?

281
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:40,040
I'm a photographer,
so of course I'd have negatives!

282
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:45,360
The person with the woman
in these pictures...

283
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:48,120
It's the American Senator,
Dickson, isn't it?

284
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:49,820
That's fine, isn't it?

285
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:52,380
Aren't those the same
negatives as Otaka's?

286
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:55,940
By "the same," do you mean the ones
that were missing from the victim's corpse?

287
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:58,480
-So if you have those…
-Saginuma...

288
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:02,380
Did you kill Otaka and
then steal these negatives?

289
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:06,380
These are mine!
I took these together with Otaka!

290
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:09,220
They turned out worse
than Otaka’s but…

291
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,880
I was planning to sell them
to a newspaper, too.

292
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:14,440
You guys heard Otaka
talking about that, right?

293
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:19,700
Well, it wasn't me!

294
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:22,740
Well, if you are suspect me,
then bring out the murder weapon!

295
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,900
The criminal should still have
the murder weapon, right?!

296
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:27,740
But the murder weapon
hasn't been found anywhere yet.

297
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:30,680
There’s still a place where
we can find the murder weapon.

298
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,680
We did the body checks
just now, right?!

299
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:33,780
No.

300
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,940
The most important place
has been overlooked.

301
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:38,400
The most important place?!

302
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:40,800
The murdered Otaka's luggage.

303
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:43,720
That's all that's left.

304
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,200
Here.

305
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,260
Ah, which is Otaka's luggage?

306
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:55,940
-Is something the matter?
-Ah, no...

307
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:59,960
I just remember when he had left his bag
behind at his studio one week ago...

308
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:03,300
It had been cut to shreds
with sharp object...

309
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:08,500
So I bought him
a new bag for travel.

310
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:13,280
I think it's possible that the 
negatives were in his previous bag...

311
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:15,680
...and someone may have
searching for them, right?

312
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,360
Yes.

313
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,100
There doesn't seem
to be anything here...

314
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:31,700
...that could be used as
the murder weapon.

315
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:36,320
This is after all, just the deduction of
a high-school student playing detective.

316
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:39,300
<i>What is with this case...</i>

317
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,820
<i>If the murder weapon
can't be found...</i>

318
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:45,100
<i>...I also won't be able to
figure out when Otaka was killed.</i>

319
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:48,340
Is someone giving
a false testimony...?

320
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:52,640
Like I thought, you're
the criminal, aren't you?

321
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:55,240
Huh?
What are you saying?

322
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:59,140
When this lady was asking
the stewardess for the medicine...

323
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:02,860
...you weren't in the seat
behind the sleeping Otaka.

324
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:07,260
Just a minute! I was awake when
the stewardess brought the medicine...

325
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:09,640
...but Saginuma was sleeping
in the seat behind, right?

326
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:12,720
-Otaka was gone, though...
-There, see! Stop bullshitting!

327
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:15,640
But, even this stewardess
saw that, right?

328
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:19,140
Yes. I don't think he was there...

329
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:20,960
Hey, what are you two suggesting?!

330
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:23,920
Let's hear from the stewardess
who brought the medicine as well.

331
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:26,040
At the time Tsugumi asked
for the medicine...

332
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,980
...was this person in the
seat behind Otaka?

333
00:19:29,260 --> 00:19:31,320
I was fast asleep, right?
Right!

334
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:35,980
Whether he was there or
whether he wasn't there...

335
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:39,500
-Otaka was there, wasn't he?
-That I do remember.

336
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:42,500
He was asleep, with an eye
mask and blanket put on.

337
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,920
Was there anyone in front of Otaka?

338
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:49,420
As I recall, there wasn't...

339
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:56,160
I know!

340
00:19:58,040 --> 00:20:02,480
<i>Saginuma's seat was,
if I remember...Right here.</i>

341
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,080
<i>I knew it!</i>

342
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:21,000
<i>There's no mistake.
The criminal is that person!</i>

343
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:25,940
What happened all of a sudden?

344
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:28,640
What do you mean?
I know who the criminal is.

345
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,340
Eh? No way!?

346
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:34,900
All that's left is the
mysterious murder weapon.

347
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:38,400
Are you okay?

348
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:41,900
I'm fine, but...

349
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:47,440
Ah! No, no! You're wrong!

350
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:50,400
Hey! Where were
you touching me!?

351
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:52,320
It wasn't on purpose!

352
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:54,140
<i>Still, they are bigger than
I thought they were.</i>

353
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:56,440
<i>Since Ran is a high school student.</i>

354
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:00,140
Shinichi, you pervert!

355
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:04,640
That’s not what I meant...

356
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:08,880
I wanted to ask you this since you
have became a high school student...

357
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:18,480
Huh?
Wait... What is it...

358
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:22,380
Hurry and tell me.
I'm embarrassed for even asking it.

359
00:21:26,220 --> 00:21:30,520
Most of them are like this lately...

360
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:38,060
-I see. So that's it...
-Huh?! How did that convince you?

361
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:39,980
I've figured it out at last.

362
00:21:40,220 --> 00:21:43,960
The criminal's trump card for
how they ended the victim's life...

363
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:48,300
The trick of the murder weapon!

364
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:49,900
Chizuru.

365
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:53,460
Is it true that there was a returning
knock from the restroom?

366
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,800
Why do I need to lie about that?

367
00:21:55,920 --> 00:22:00,260
Because it seems that you went to the
restroom after Otaka who was murdered.

368
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:03,440
In other words, she didn't lie.

369
00:22:03,660 --> 00:22:05,580
When Chizuru knocked...

370
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,360
...there was someone else in the
restroom with the victim's corpse...

371
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:09,140
...other than the criminal.

372
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:12,080
-Eh?!
-Please remember.

373
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:13,620
There were bloodstains scattered...

374
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:17,180
...on the wall of the restroom that
got there during the time of the crime.

375
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:21,240
And yet, on the back of the body
which was leaning against the wall...

376
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:23,240
...there was no blood.

377
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:28,580
That was because the blood from the time
of Otaka's murder had dried on the wall...

378
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:31,960
And that someone other than the
criminal then moved his body afterwards.

379
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:35,040
Why was the body moved?

380
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:39,720
That's because they were
looking for those negatives...

381
00:22:39,940 --> 00:22:43,120
...that Otaka should have
had on him.

382
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:47,540
Isn't that right...Mr. Edward?

383
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:54,460
When you were looking
for the negatives...

384
00:22:54,580 --> 00:22:56,440
...you also checked
the pockets of his pants.

385
00:22:56,780 --> 00:23:01,260
That was when the cologne on
your wrist got stuck to his pockets.

386
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:05,340
So in a rush, you washed your
hands and wet a handkerchief.

387
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:08,440
You then used that to wipe away
the unique smell from the pocket.

388
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:13,540
The only evidence
of that is your wrist...

389
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,800
It doesn't have cologne on it.

390
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:18,840
Edward...

391
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:22,800
You can actually
speak Japanese, can you?

392
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:26,960
Hurry and speak it
for your own sake.

393
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:39,460
-It's as this boy says.
-Eh?! He spoke Japanese!

394
00:23:39,740 --> 00:23:43,540
The scandal photos
taken of Senator Dickson.

395
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:47,420
I was asked to purchase the negatives.

396
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,160
When I heard that he had
gone to the restroom...

397
00:23:50,340 --> 00:23:53,580
...I thought that would be
a chance to do a trade with him.

398
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:57,020
But he was dead.

399
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:00,740
He was bent over at the waist.

400
00:24:02,620 --> 00:24:05,340
Though I thought
it was wrong of me...

401
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:08,980
I searched his body
for the negatives.

402
00:24:09,420 --> 00:24:12,900
<i>Then, when I knocked,
the one who answered...</i>

403
00:24:13,060 --> 00:24:15,100
<i>Otaka, are you okay?</i>

404
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:17,200
I was surprised at the time.

405
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:21,760
No matter how much I looked for
them, I couldn't find those negatives.

406
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:26,180
Edward and Chizuru,
who knocked from outside...

407
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:28,860
...can't be considered
as the criminals.

408
00:24:29,580 --> 00:24:33,960
That leaves 2 remaining suspects,
Ukai and Tsugumi.

409
00:24:34,220 --> 00:24:35,540
Eh?!

410
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:39,000
What bothered me was
Ukai's testimony.

411
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:41,280
At the time Tsugumi
was asking for the medicine...

412
00:24:41,460 --> 00:24:45,960
He says Saginuma wasn't in
his seat behind the victim, Otaka.

413
00:24:46,460 --> 00:24:49,760
Well... I wasn't lying!
Even the stewardess saw that!

414
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:51,620
And I said I was asleep!

415
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:54,540
Neither of you two are lying.

416
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:57,780
It was the differing testimony
between you two...

417
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:01,780
...has provided an important
clue to finding the criminal.

418
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,580
Then you know
who the criminal is?

419
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:05,960
Who is it?

420
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:14,400
The criminal who
murdered Otaka was...

421
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,820
Tsugumi...you.

422
00:25:25,120 --> 00:25:26,420
Eh?

423
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:30,300
You've gotta be joking!

424
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:32,720
Evidence!
Where's your evidence?!

425
00:25:32,980 --> 00:25:34,920
There is proper evidence.

426
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:38,520
Because Tsugumi should still have
the murder weapon on her.

427
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:41,780
Tsugumi took the physical
search too, didn't she?

428
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:47,500
The weapon used to murder Otaka
wouldn't be considered suspicious.

429
00:25:47,660 --> 00:25:50,580
It would also pass through the
metal detector at a boarding gate...

430
00:25:50,740 --> 00:25:52,460
...and is a thing
only made for women.

431
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:54,080
Only made for women?

432
00:25:54,220 --> 00:25:56,600
No, no, there couldn't be such
a convenient thing, could there?

433
00:25:56,780 --> 00:25:58,200
There is.

434
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:02,460
It's Tsugumi's...

435
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:04,600
Ah! I know!

436
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:06,600
Yes.

437
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:11,040
The wire from the underwear
of Tsugumi's right breast.

438
00:26:11,420 --> 00:26:14,100
-Underwear wire?!
-No, no...

439
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:16,700
It'd be impossible to kill
someone with something like that!

440
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:18,700
The wire had been
sharpened ahead of time...

441
00:26:18,860 --> 00:26:20,220
...and then stabbed into
the back of his head.

442
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:21,940
Multiplied using the weight
from her entire body...

443
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:24,240
...it would reach
the cervical spinal cord.

444
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:26,920
It's a crime that even
a woman could commit.

445
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:29,820
The reason why the wire
wasn’t disposed of is...

446
00:26:29,980 --> 00:26:32,420
...because should it be known
to be the murder weapon.

447
00:26:32,540 --> 00:26:34,260
The woman without a wire
in her underwear...

448
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:36,740
...would have been
exposed as the criminal.

449
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:41,380
If so...If Tsugumi takes another
body check, it would be fine, right?

450
00:26:41,820 --> 00:26:44,620
It's no use, Saginuma...

451
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:48,260
If they searched me again
they'd find out right away...

452
00:26:48,860 --> 00:26:50,620
You...

453
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:53,380
Tsugumi...

454
00:26:54,380 --> 00:26:58,480
To start off, Tsugumi was in the seat
next to the sleeping Chizuru...

455
00:26:58,660 --> 00:27:01,060
...when Otaka went to the restroom.

456
00:27:02,880 --> 00:27:06,600
And then, just as he
opened the door...

457
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:09,440
He was hit with a handkerchief
soaked in chemicals...

458
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,280
...and soon lost consciousness.

459
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:14,560
Removing the wire from
her underwear...

460
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:16,940
...she pierced Otaka's
cervical spinal cord.

461
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:19,420
Asphyxiating him to death.

462
00:27:20,660 --> 00:27:24,700
That scratch wound on
his body was caused by...

463
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:28,580
...the end that hadn't been
sharpened, wasn't it?

464
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:31,900
To make it look as though the crime
had been over the negatives...

465
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:35,020
You used the scissors from your
sewing kit to cut up the negatives...

466
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:37,740
...and then flushed
them down the toilet.

467
00:27:38,780 --> 00:27:41,760
And, when Tsugumi had returned
from the restroom to her seat...

468
00:27:41,920 --> 00:27:48,920
She disguised Saginuma as Otaka
using a knit hat and eye mask.

469
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:51,760
Ma’am, can I help you?

470
00:27:52,060 --> 00:27:53,220
I'm sorry.

471
00:27:53,420 --> 00:27:55,120
Do you have medicine
for motion sickness?

472
00:27:55,300 --> 00:27:57,360
Yes. Please wait just a moment.

473
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:07,920
That's why Ukai could mistake the
disguised Saginuma for being Otaka.

474
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:13,280
By doing that, Tsugumi created 
an illusion for the time...

475
00:28:13,420 --> 00:28:15,060
...when Otaka had gone
to the restroom.

476
00:28:15,300 --> 00:28:16,200
Are you okay?

477
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:18,060
It was a dark cabin and...

478
00:28:18,220 --> 00:28:20,960
...all that was sticking out from
the blanket was his nose and up.

479
00:28:21,360 --> 00:28:23,480
It's reasonable for such
a misunderstanding.

480
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,940
Ah, the medicine is for her.

481
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:29,480
The evidence that Tsugumi used the
trick of disguising Saginuma was...

482
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:34,100
...this piece of negative that had
fallen into the seat next to him.

483
00:28:35,360 --> 00:28:38,380
If a piece had gotten stuck to her clothes
while she was cutting up the negatives...

484
00:28:38,540 --> 00:28:40,940
It would fall off when she was
setting up the disguise, wouldn't it?

485
00:28:41,140 --> 00:28:43,940
Then, that empty seat that I saw...

486
00:28:44,180 --> 00:28:47,880
The seat behind Saginuma was free,
so you misunderstood.

487
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:50,620
What if the seat next to
me hadn't been vacant?

488
00:28:50,860 --> 00:28:53,280
In that case making such a disguise
would have been impossible!

489
00:28:53,600 --> 00:28:57,440
Tsugumi, you had the seat next to him
reserved and didn't cancel it, did you?

490
00:28:58,100 --> 00:29:01,400
By doing so, she would be certain
to ensure a vacant seat next to him.

491
00:29:01,660 --> 00:29:02,700
How could anyone
possibly sleep through...

492
00:29:02,820 --> 00:29:05,880
...having a hat and eye mask
put on them and not wake up?

493
00:29:06,240 --> 00:29:09,860
If the drug to prevent motion sickness
given to Saginuma by Tsugumi was....

494
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:13,600
...a sleeping pill,
he wouldn't have awakened easily.

495
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:18,180
A knit hat like Otaka's was
also in Tsugumi's luggage.

496
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:22,640
If she remembers Otaka’s sleeping
posture, there wouldn't be a problem.

497
00:29:23,420 --> 00:29:25,140
No way...

498
00:29:26,040 --> 00:29:27,700
Tsugumi...

499
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:29,260
Why?

500
00:29:31,500 --> 00:29:36,020
It’s because of the Grand Prize photo
of the fire incident which he took.

501
00:29:36,440 --> 00:29:40,840
But it was that photo that made both
of you into seeing one another.

502
00:29:41,040 --> 00:29:42,500
That's right.

503
00:29:42,760 --> 00:29:45,220
Because of that photo,
I became interested in him.

504
00:29:46,700 --> 00:29:51,340
The first time I saw his photo,
my heart quivered.

505
00:29:52,420 --> 00:29:57,940
The fear and tragedy of a fire and…

506
00:29:58,140 --> 00:30:00,200
...the preciousness of life.

507
00:30:01,180 --> 00:30:03,960
He was a person who could
express all that in a photo.

508
00:30:04,180 --> 00:30:05,300
In that case, why then!?

509
00:30:05,460 --> 00:30:08,220
Because of that photo, my older
brother's life was taken away!

510
00:30:10,740 --> 00:30:14,980
Could it be that
Otaka himself set that fire...?

511
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:17,440
Yes.

512
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:24,100
It had come from his apartment.

513
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:30,980
The amount of smoke rising up
to my brother's apartment...

514
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:33,340
...increased by the moment.

515
00:30:39,180 --> 00:30:41,800
I didn't believe it at first.

516
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:47,680
But, when I asked him about it...

517
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:49,400
He bragged about it.

518
00:30:49,580 --> 00:30:53,180
A good moment never comes no matter
how long I had been waiting for it.

519
00:30:53,900 --> 00:30:56,600
Unless I made it myself!

520
00:30:57,560 --> 00:31:00,960
Brother! Brother!

521
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,920
I could never forgive him.

522
00:31:09,740 --> 00:31:12,280
That's why...

523
00:31:26,740 --> 00:31:29,100
But this is vexing.

524
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:41,500
I was confident that
I had hidden the weapon.

525
00:31:42,620 --> 00:31:45,440
When you reached up
for Otaka’s luggage...

526
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:48,660
For some reason you displayed
some unnatural movement.

527
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:53,620
When I remembered that,
I was convinced.

528
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:57,800
The sharpened point of the wire
was touching your skin...

529
00:31:57,920 --> 00:32:00,220
...causing you to hesitate
unconsciously.

530
00:32:01,700 --> 00:32:04,000
Just that?

531
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:06,920
It wasn't a big thing.

532
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:10,240
But what should have
been just a casual act...

533
00:32:10,380 --> 00:32:13,760
...looked unnatural in my eyes
and remained in my memory.

534
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:17,040
It's the small points
which can be overlooked.

535
00:32:17,380 --> 00:32:19,260
That are the most
important points of all.

536
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:27,320
What's this?

537
00:32:27,760 --> 00:32:30,040
Acting all great...

538
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:34,420
Thing is, touching a person's
chest to find a clue like that...

539
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:38,500
That's totally sexual harassment!
That's totally sexual harassment!

540
00:32:39,300 --> 00:32:41,920
Hey! What are you
saying out of the blue!

541
00:32:42,060 --> 00:32:43,160
Eh?!

542
00:32:43,500 --> 00:32:45,360
I... was sleeping?

543
00:32:46,760 --> 00:32:49,020
Ah, oh no!

544
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:53,080
It’s nothing! It’s nothing.
Sorry.

545
00:32:57,220 --> 00:33:02,020
"Kyoto The Film Studio Mystery Case"

546
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:05,460
I ended up embarrassed
because of you sleep talking.

547
00:33:05,660 --> 00:33:08,820
"Kyoto"
How persistent! I couldn't help it...

548
00:33:08,980 --> 00:33:12,140
Because we took that flight a year ago
and this one had the same feel to it...

549
00:33:12,280 --> 00:33:15,260
So I unintentionally
had a dream about it.

550
00:33:15,740 --> 00:33:17,660
Is this really the right road?

551
00:33:17,980 --> 00:33:19,600
If we keep going just as we are...

552
00:33:19,780 --> 00:33:21,740
...we'll just arrive at the Sangoji temple,
famous for its sakura trees.

553
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:25,520
It says that this is a shortcut.

554
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:28,300
That's strange.

555
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:31,520
Perhaps it's around here...

556
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:37,560
Ah! Aren't these...

557
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:41,220
Lucky Bookmarks that
have been so fashionable lately?

558
00:33:41,360 --> 00:33:44,700
-Lucky Bookmarks?
-I don't know all the details...

559
00:33:44,860 --> 00:33:48,460
But they seem to be pretty
popular on TV and in magazines.

560
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:51,380
-I don't know all the details though.
-Is that right?

561
00:33:52,140 --> 00:33:55,600
Since we happened to pass by
chance, couldn't we take a little look?

562
00:33:55,900 --> 00:33:59,380
-Right! Right!
-Well, we don't have time...

563
00:34:00,140 --> 00:34:01,860
Welcome!

564
00:34:02,060 --> 00:34:04,060
Our store's lucky bookmarks
brings to both single people...

565
00:34:04,220 --> 00:34:07,000
...and couples and of course you.

566
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:09,160
With the nice atmosphere
of being a couple...

567
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:12,440
...and are an extremely popular
matchmaking product.

568
00:34:12,720 --> 00:34:14,200
-Matchmaking?
-Yes.

569
00:34:14,340 --> 00:34:17,900
Is that right? I didn't know
anything about that.

570
00:34:18,280 --> 00:34:21,560
How about this
sakura-colored bookmark?

571
00:34:22,020 --> 00:34:24,380
They're available for
a limited 2 week period...

572
00:34:24,540 --> 00:34:26,500
...and will only be sold
until tomorrow.

573
00:34:26,700 --> 00:34:28,580
Just like with a normal bookmark...

574
00:34:28,740 --> 00:34:32,020
...it's also possible to affix
your names on them.

575
00:34:32,300 --> 00:34:35,640
-Ah...
-What should we do?

576
00:34:36,720 --> 00:34:37,840
Fool.

577
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:41,040
There's no way I could buy
matchmaking goods.

578
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:44,320
Ah, here, here!
I've been looking for these!

579
00:34:44,500 --> 00:34:47,540
Hey Mama, since I want to bring
a souvenir for everyone in my class...

580
00:34:47,700 --> 00:34:48,840
...please buy me these.

581
00:34:48,980 --> 00:34:50,960
Well, can't be helped.

582
00:34:51,240 --> 00:34:54,060
Say, weren't you guys
gonna buy some?

583
00:34:54,460 --> 00:34:57,120
Ah, that's okay.
We'll buy some later.

584
00:34:57,300 --> 00:34:59,940
-Right?!
-Eh? Yeah..

585
00:35:00,140 --> 00:35:01,940
Then that's fine!

586
00:35:03,100 --> 00:35:06,520
"Merchandise Sold Out"
It's too bad.

587
00:35:06,660 --> 00:35:10,080
That girl bought up all of them.

588
00:35:10,420 --> 00:35:14,100
We’ll have new stocks
again in the evening.

589
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:18,760
"Welcome - Kyoto Futomaki Film Studio"

590
00:35:21,420 --> 00:35:23,460
It's more incredible than I thought.

591
00:35:23,780 --> 00:35:26,120
They've even reproduced
the old townscape of Kyoto.

592
00:35:26,300 --> 00:35:27,940
Maybe so!

593
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:30,140
Why? Are you still angry?

594
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:33,820
Not really.
I'm not angry!

595
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:36,820
Is it this way?

596
00:35:37,580 --> 00:35:40,360
Geez! Shinichi!

597
00:35:41,340 --> 00:35:44,060
"Sakuraba, You'll Be Killed"

598
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:50,740
Who was it that sent me
such a thing!?

599
00:35:50,980 --> 00:35:52,540
It's just a common
harassment letter.

600
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:54,440
I'm sure it's from a Momoka fan.

601
00:35:54,580 --> 00:35:56,520
It was put in the dressing room.

602
00:35:56,820 --> 00:35:59,880
It's likely that it was the act
of someone working here!

603
00:36:00,120 --> 00:36:01,840
Damn!

604
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:04,700
They just envy my popularity.

605
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:18,360
Hey, stop this!

606
00:36:18,620 --> 00:36:22,120
-We're over already!
-I'm worried.

607
00:36:22,740 --> 00:36:25,700
-Isn't this okay?
-Wait...

608
00:36:25,900 --> 00:36:28,960
Ryoma has Oryo, doesn't he?

609
00:36:29,700 --> 00:36:31,900
Don’t worry about Momoka!

610
00:36:32,300 --> 00:36:36,480
I just went out with
that woman for publicity sake.

611
00:36:37,940 --> 00:36:40,040
I guess for me...

612
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:42,960
It has to be you...

613
00:36:58,040 --> 00:36:59,700
What are you doing?!

614
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,840
You were behaving strangely lately...

615
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:04,180
But it seems that you're cheating
on me with your ex-girlfriend!

616
00:37:04,980 --> 00:37:07,280
Do you know who you have
to thank for this role?

617
00:37:08,320 --> 00:37:12,060
If you are going to do this,
then I'm going to ruin this film!

618
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:14,100
Get ready.

619
00:37:18,880 --> 00:37:22,800
-Hey. Chase after her.
-Why?

620
00:37:23,020 --> 00:37:26,520
She might be serious
about ruining this film.

621
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:29,100
I wouldn't want that.

622
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:33,380
Even if it's just a small role,
I want to finish it properly.

623
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:52,180
All right. It'll be okay
if I go after her, right?

624
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:01,680
Sorry for the interruption.

625
00:38:01,920 --> 00:38:04,380
We didn't mean to eavesdrop or anything.

626
00:38:04,620 --> 00:38:08,820
Where is the shooting spot for the 
historical movie, "Ryoma's Holiday"?

627
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:11,880
-We've gotten lost...
-Ah, that would be here.

628
00:38:12,300 --> 00:38:13,720
Excuse us.

629
00:38:15,940 --> 00:38:20,260
-Ah, you dropped this.
-Ah, thank you.

630
00:38:20,700 --> 00:38:23,520
-Here.
-Ah, thank you very much.

631
00:38:25,760 --> 00:38:30,760
Hey! Wasn't she with the Idol
Hayashibara Momoka and...

632
00:38:30,900 --> 00:38:33,020
...the actor Sakuraba Reiichi
just now?

633
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:34,600
Sakuraba Reiichi?

634
00:38:34,760 --> 00:38:37,280
Look, it’s the topic everyone’s
been discussing for a while.

635
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:38,800
Those two have been
seeing each other.

636
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:40,460
It had been covered on
the "Friday" show.

637
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:44,920
It’s true that that they’re
passionately in love!

638
00:38:45,140 --> 00:38:47,060
You’re a celebrity nerd...

639
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:55,000
"Role of Nakaoka Shintaro, Iwasaki Ryuji"

640
00:38:57,100 --> 00:38:59,420
Oh, what's the matter, Momoka?

641
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:02,740
Could it be you quarreled with
Sakuraba? He's been cocky recently.

642
00:39:02,900 --> 00:39:05,780
Disgusting!
Don't talk to me so casually!

643
00:39:05,940 --> 00:39:07,520
That's dangerous!

644
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:16,040
I have never seen
a movie set like this before.

645
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:19,540
It's pretty dusty, isn't it?

646
00:39:28,460 --> 00:39:32,020
Shinichi! Are you okay?!

647
00:39:32,180 --> 00:39:33,880
No, no...
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

648
00:39:34,060 --> 00:39:36,420
I raised the sword and
it just slipped out of my hands.

649
00:39:37,920 --> 00:39:38,960
What are you guys doing here?!

650
00:39:39,100 --> 00:39:41,380
And after all the trouble we went
through to see you, Uncle!

651
00:39:41,540 --> 00:39:45,640
Hey, Dad! If you're not really careful,
there'll be a horrible accident!

652
00:39:46,320 --> 00:39:50,280
Uncle, you need to hold
your sword properly or...

653
00:39:50,460 --> 00:39:51,820
It's Doyle!?

654
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:55,780
-Ran, you came!
-Kazuha! It's been a while.

655
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:59,220
Huh, huh? What's this?
You guys know each other?

656
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:02,060
We solved a case
together once before.

657
00:40:02,220 --> 00:40:06,320
Yeah. I showed Doyle here
my brilliant deductions. Right, Doyle?

658
00:40:07,040 --> 00:40:10,820
-This guy's name is Kudo...
-Do, do...The nickname Doyle…

659
00:40:11,020 --> 00:40:14,120
-I'm turning down this role!
-What are you saying?!

660
00:40:14,380 --> 00:40:18,000
Don't say that Momoka won't
perform the role of Oryo!

661
00:40:18,220 --> 00:40:19,440
Because!

662
00:40:19,580 --> 00:40:21,940
The acting in the Ryoma role
doesn't match up with mine.

663
00:40:22,260 --> 00:40:26,360
That's why either I go or you
change who's playing Ryoma.

664
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:28,720
Yes!

665
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:33,320
For the role of Sakamoto Ryoma,
please give it to me, Mori Kogoro.

666
00:40:33,560 --> 00:40:34,440
Uncle!

667
00:40:34,580 --> 00:40:36,720
Read the atmosphere around you!

668
00:40:37,420 --> 00:40:38,860
That's right!

669
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:41,760
Fumiko could be my replacement?

670
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:44,340
Ryoma seems to like you as well.

671
00:40:44,660 --> 00:40:46,340
No...

672
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:49,840
Do you think you're some princess?

673
00:40:50,060 --> 00:40:51,360
I have the leading role!

674
00:40:51,480 --> 00:40:53,480
That leading role was
thanks to me, wasn't it?

675
00:40:53,660 --> 00:40:56,960
Yes, yes. This movie, is thanks
to Momoka's popularity...

676
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:59,620
...and it also concerns
our sponsors. Right?

677
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:01,600
Minor roles should keep quiet!

678
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:04,680
Anyway, I am quitting the role!

679
00:41:07,820 --> 00:41:09,780
You guys...

680
00:41:09,980 --> 00:41:13,520
At this rate, the schedule
will be a mess…

681
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:16,120
Somehow, this is a disturbing
atmosphere, isn't it?

682
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:19,580
That Idol's selfishness is
the cause of this.

683
00:41:19,740 --> 00:41:22,220
Isn't this a lover's quarrel
between Sakuraba and her?

684
00:41:22,420 --> 00:41:24,720
It seems that those two are
seeing each other after all?

685
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:27,860
Talk about Sakuraba and Momoka
has raised their popularity.

686
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:32,180
It seems that the leading role went to
him because of Momoka's support.

687
00:41:32,540 --> 00:41:36,100
I read in a weekly magazine
that handsome actor...

688
00:41:36,300 --> 00:41:39,200
...has even insured his own face.

689
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:41,060
Hmpf! That narcissist.

690
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:43,980
-I heard about that, too.
-Me, too.

691
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:46,500
Uncle, what are you doing?

692
00:41:47,280 --> 00:41:49,800
An actor's face is their life.

693
00:42:05,060 --> 00:42:06,620
I am pissed!

694
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:20,460
You idiot, Sakuraba, 
angering Momoka like that.

695
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:24,800
If a popular Idol turns down her
role, my head will fall off first!

696
00:42:24,940 --> 00:42:26,400
I'm sorry!

697
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:29,460
"Assistant Director: Tanaka Taiki"

698
00:42:30,240 --> 00:42:31,940
"Movie Director: Kashimoto Yoshihiro"

699
00:42:39,340 --> 00:42:43,100
"Popular Idol Hayashibara Momoka and
Hot Actor Inside a Car Making Love!"

700
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:59,100
Yes. Everyone, thank you for waiting.
We will be shooting scene 44.

701
00:42:59,260 --> 00:43:01,020
Please stand by!

702
00:43:01,380 --> 00:43:03,040
If you would please.

703
00:43:04,140 --> 00:43:07,200
Uncle, do you really want
to go with that look?

704
00:43:07,520 --> 00:43:11,260
-Huh? You have a problem?
-The mustache...Mustache!

705
00:43:11,400 --> 00:43:13,680
The Shinsengumi wouldn't wear
such a mustache!

706
00:43:13,920 --> 00:43:15,740
This is my trademark!

707
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:18,700
No matter what happens,
I can't shave it off!

708
00:43:20,180 --> 00:43:23,200
-Fight just like we rehearsed.
-Yes!

709
00:43:23,860 --> 00:43:26,120
Then Sakuraba, if you would.

710
00:43:29,100 --> 00:43:30,960
Yes. Is everything okay?

711
00:43:31,220 --> 00:43:32,660
Yes, then Director,
if you would please.

712
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:33,760
If you would please.

713
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:36,020
-Then this is the main take!
-Main take!

714
00:43:36,340 --> 00:43:37,660
Okay!

715
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:39,720
Start!

716
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:45,500
It's the Shinsengumi!
Hurry and run!

717
00:43:54,800 --> 00:43:57,140
For the sake of official business!

718
00:44:05,400 --> 00:44:07,000
Sakamoto!

719
00:44:09,180 --> 00:44:10,620
Prepare yourself.

720
00:44:11,660 --> 00:44:14,720
Just when you said that the
dawn of Japan is right before us...

721
00:44:15,260 --> 00:44:16,500
Come.

722
00:44:16,760 --> 00:44:19,020
I, Nakaoka Shintaro,
will be your opponent.

723
00:44:21,300 --> 00:44:23,520
Watch out!
Watch out you fools!

724
00:44:26,880 --> 00:44:28,860
Watch out, I said!

725
00:44:28,980 --> 00:44:32,100
Those swords aren't real, right?

726
00:44:32,520 --> 00:44:34,540
That’s impossible, they're fakes.

727
00:44:34,820 --> 00:44:37,040
But those sparks...

728
00:44:37,380 --> 00:44:39,880
There's a device in the sword
that allows electricity...

729
00:44:40,040 --> 00:44:42,220
...to flow out like sparks from them.

730
00:44:42,820 --> 00:44:46,020
As expected of Doyle.
You know a lot, don't you?

731
00:44:46,200 --> 00:44:48,060
You're just like a detective.

732
00:44:48,800 --> 00:44:51,460
I just knew it coincidentally.
That’s all.

733
00:45:01,160 --> 00:45:03,900
-Nakaoka!
-Ryoma!

734
00:45:04,180 --> 00:45:06,380
The rest is up to you...

735
00:45:10,680 --> 00:45:12,060
Okita!

736
00:45:12,240 --> 00:45:13,600
But I can still go on!

737
00:45:21,020 --> 00:45:22,980
I can still go on!

738
00:45:25,500 --> 00:45:26,720
This is bad!

739
00:45:26,960 --> 00:45:29,180
Hattori! Uncle!
Run!

740
00:45:39,620 --> 00:45:41,100
My face!

741
00:45:41,280 --> 00:45:44,660
-My face!
-Reiichi! Reiichi!

742
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:47,540
Reiichi!

743
00:45:48,080 --> 00:45:49,720
Uncle!

744
00:45:50,940 --> 00:45:53,160
Hattori!

745
00:45:53,600 --> 00:45:56,740
An ambulance! Someone please
call for an ambulance!

746
00:45:58,720 --> 00:46:00,540
Dad, here?

747
00:46:13,180 --> 00:46:15,960
Heiji...

748
00:46:22,600 --> 00:46:26,720
Hattori's unconscious.
Uncle is refusing visitors.

749
00:46:28,340 --> 00:46:30,260
How could this...

750
00:46:30,680 --> 00:46:32,940
What are you doing here?

751
00:46:33,320 --> 00:46:34,920
You and Reiichi are over, aren't you?

752
00:46:35,220 --> 00:46:36,980
Why are you coming to the hospital for?

753
00:46:37,160 --> 00:46:39,680
I was just worried about Sakuraba...

754
00:46:39,800 --> 00:46:41,400
You say such things...

755
00:46:41,580 --> 00:46:44,080
But honestly, you only want to
get back with him, don't you?

756
00:46:44,340 --> 00:46:46,880
Just because your ex-boyfriend
became popular.

757
00:46:47,040 --> 00:46:50,120
-Shameful.
-That's not...

758
00:46:50,800 --> 00:46:52,500
Don't misunderstand.

759
00:46:54,240 --> 00:46:57,580
A supporting actor like you
wouldn't be a match for him.

760
00:46:57,800 --> 00:46:58,860
Sakuraba!

761
00:46:59,080 --> 00:47:02,980
Even with such a minor burn, you
should rest for at least a little longer...

762
00:47:03,460 --> 00:47:04,960
You two stop this.

763
00:47:05,300 --> 00:47:07,440
I could hear you from
the consultation room.

764
00:47:07,900 --> 00:47:09,680
What's with tone of voice?

765
00:47:10,740 --> 00:47:13,300
After I followed you here
to the hospital.

766
00:47:13,920 --> 00:47:16,420
Will your injury be okay?

767
00:47:19,580 --> 00:47:21,540
It's nothing much...

768
00:47:23,080 --> 00:47:25,460
But it is painful as an actor.

769
00:47:26,880 --> 00:47:28,620
What will happen to your role?

770
00:47:29,060 --> 00:47:31,020
After getting the lead role...

771
00:47:31,260 --> 00:47:35,900
I'll have to talk with the Director and
see whether they'll resume with the shoot.

772
00:47:38,740 --> 00:47:42,040
What a fool! What shoot?

773
00:47:45,940 --> 00:47:49,360
Without me, no one
would work with you!

774
00:47:49,840 --> 00:47:52,680
So why don’t you two
get together as unpopular actors...

775
00:48:05,640 --> 00:48:09,280
"Sakuraba, You'll Be Killed"

776
00:48:13,720 --> 00:48:18,200
For now, we are back
at the village set but...

777
00:48:18,360 --> 00:48:21,040
...the shoot might be canceled, right?

778
00:48:21,320 --> 00:48:23,920
With such an explosive accident.

779
00:48:25,340 --> 00:48:27,560
It couldn’t be just an accident.

780
00:48:31,980 --> 00:48:35,600
-Are you Shinichi Kudo?
-Yes. That's right...

781
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:38,860
I'm Inugai of Kyoto's Prefectural police.

782
00:48:40,220 --> 00:48:41,620
"Kyoto Prefectural Police Detective
- Hajime Inugai"

783
00:48:41,800 --> 00:48:43,940
Oh, sorry, sorry.

784
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:47,720
Well...

785
00:48:47,940 --> 00:48:50,080
I've heard a lot about you!

786
00:48:50,320 --> 00:48:54,280
One year ago, you splendidly settled
that case on that airliner, didn't you?

787
00:48:54,400 --> 00:48:56,140
That was something.

788
00:48:56,880 --> 00:48:57,800
Ah...

789
00:48:58,020 --> 00:49:00,400
I'd like to hear about
that story sometime...

790
00:49:00,820 --> 00:49:03,440
Sure, but before that,
I would like to study the scene.

791
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:07,300
-Oh, oh, right! Ah, which way?
-This way.

792
00:49:09,520 --> 00:49:11,980
-Are you a Detective?
-Yes.

793
00:49:15,140 --> 00:49:17,840
I have something to tell you.

794
00:49:18,540 --> 00:49:24,180
Hmm...Sakuraba was sent
a threatening letter, huh...

795
00:49:24,840 --> 00:49:27,920
Does Sakuraba have any ideas
about who it might be?

796
00:49:28,940 --> 00:49:32,800
He was an action actor who
wasn't popular for a long time...

797
00:49:33,140 --> 00:49:36,400
But he met Momoka on a set one day...

798
00:49:37,420 --> 00:49:42,180
And then she introduced
him to various producers...

799
00:49:42,340 --> 00:49:43,980
...and he started picking up
jobs one after another.

800
00:49:44,160 --> 00:49:46,960
Well, thanks to his lover
he became a star.

801
00:49:47,220 --> 00:49:49,660
No surprise that many would
be jealous of him, correct?

802
00:49:49,800 --> 00:49:51,400
Please stop talking that way.

803
00:49:51,540 --> 00:49:53,960
He's been working hard
all this time at it.

804
00:49:54,520 --> 00:49:58,000
Now to have an injury to his face...

805
00:49:58,760 --> 00:49:59,800
Not to be rude, but...

806
00:49:59,940 --> 00:50:02,300
...what sort of relationship
do you have with Sakuraba?

807
00:50:03,120 --> 00:50:05,960
We're just colleagues from
the same theatre group.

808
00:50:06,180 --> 00:50:09,640
That's why I became anxious
about that threatening letter.

809
00:50:10,520 --> 00:50:12,080
Is that right?

810
00:50:12,920 --> 00:50:17,660
Please see to it that Sakuraba
doesn't come into any further danger.

811
00:50:22,180 --> 00:50:25,520
Could it be called
an attempted murder?

812
00:50:25,720 --> 00:50:29,800
There aren’t any traces of gas
leakage or explosive material.

813
00:50:30,620 --> 00:50:33,560
What caused the explosion?

814
00:50:34,540 --> 00:50:35,680
At the time of the explosion...

815
00:50:35,820 --> 00:50:37,920
...fine particles of dust
were dancing around in this area.

816
00:50:38,100 --> 00:50:39,100
Dust?

817
00:50:39,280 --> 00:50:41,840
Dust wouldn't have anything to do
with an explosion, would it?

818
00:50:42,100 --> 00:50:43,700
A dust explosion. (Funjin bakuhatsu)

819
00:50:45,080 --> 00:50:48,280
-Explosive wind? (Fujin bakuhatsu)
-A dust explosion.

820
00:50:48,660 --> 00:50:50,480
It uses the characters for
"powder" and "dirt", so dust.

821
00:50:50,720 --> 00:50:53,300
-Well in essence, fine powder.
-Powder?

822
00:50:53,720 --> 00:50:55,980
Can such an explosion
come from powder?

823
00:50:56,260 --> 00:50:59,220
If you apply fire directly to some
powder, it wouldn't burn much.

824
00:50:59,440 --> 00:51:02,760
But once it comes in contact with
oxygen when it floats in the air...

825
00:51:02,920 --> 00:51:04,920
...it becomes flammable.

826
00:51:05,200 --> 00:51:08,120
And, if one of those particles
comes in contact with fire...

827
00:51:08,320 --> 00:51:10,300
...it spreads quickly around to
all the surrounding powder...

828
00:51:10,460 --> 00:51:12,840
...and explodes with
considerable power.

829
00:51:13,260 --> 00:51:16,600
Throwing up a cloud of dust powder
makes it easily combustible and...

830
00:51:16,780 --> 00:51:19,560
...more particularly
easy to cause an explosion.

831
00:51:20,140 --> 00:51:21,900
The criminal most likely...

832
00:51:22,620 --> 00:51:24,820
Knowing that imitation ash
would be dancing around...

833
00:51:24,940 --> 00:51:27,920
...and that the swords
would be sparking...

834
00:51:28,180 --> 00:51:30,820
...and that the fight would be
performed around the ash cloud...

835
00:51:31,020 --> 00:51:33,880
And replaced the ash
with flour or something...

836
00:51:34,260 --> 00:51:36,380
...so that it would intentionally
explode like that.

837
00:51:36,700 --> 00:51:38,740
When you consider
the threatening letter...

838
00:51:38,900 --> 00:51:42,120
The possibility that a criminal was
targeting Sakuraba would be high...

839
00:51:42,340 --> 00:51:45,940
Well then, have you made an educated
guess as to who the criminal is?

840
00:51:46,700 --> 00:51:48,320
I can't say anything
about that yet...

841
00:51:48,560 --> 00:51:50,920
...but when I consider
candidates for the criminal...

842
00:51:51,060 --> 00:51:56,220
As long as this movie has Momoka,
we'll still be able to salvage it.

843
00:51:56,680 --> 00:51:57,680
Yes.

844
00:51:59,520 --> 00:52:02,820
Yes, I understand.
Don't worry. Yes.

845
00:52:04,300 --> 00:52:06,280
Idiot Producer.

846
00:52:07,540 --> 00:52:09,480
Hey, where's Momoka?

847
00:52:11,860 --> 00:52:13,380
-Tanaka.
-Yes?

848
00:52:13,580 --> 00:52:15,080
Where's Momoka?

849
00:52:15,380 --> 00:52:17,160
Ah, she returned
from the hospital and...

850
00:52:17,320 --> 00:52:19,460
...has locked herself in
the waiting room ever since.

851
00:52:19,820 --> 00:52:21,700
Again?

852
00:52:22,260 --> 00:52:25,520
Whenever she gets in a foul mood,
she shuts herself right away.

853
00:52:26,980 --> 00:52:28,560
-Tanaka.
-Yes?

854
00:52:29,100 --> 00:52:32,140
-Go check on how she's doing.
-Understood.

855
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:45,860
Momoka.
I need to talk to you.

856
00:52:49,640 --> 00:52:52,480
Momoka?
You in there?

857
00:52:55,280 --> 00:52:57,460
But, the most suspicious person is...

858
00:52:57,640 --> 00:53:00,000
That would be Momoka, right?

859
00:53:00,140 --> 00:53:03,560
Momoka had been quarreling with
Sakuraba before the explosion.

860
00:53:03,740 --> 00:53:06,380
And was talking about
turning down her role.

861
00:53:06,920 --> 00:53:11,880
Well then, that decides it!
The criminal is Momoka!

862
00:54:00,300 --> 00:54:04,060
Momoka!
Please open the door!

863
00:54:04,480 --> 00:54:06,660
Momoka!

864
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:10,740
Hey! What's going on?

865
00:54:10,880 --> 00:54:13,840
Ah... I am Inugai from
the Kyoto Prefectural police.

866
00:54:15,640 --> 00:54:18,860
Well...The actress isn't coming
out of the waiting room.

867
00:54:19,300 --> 00:54:21,120
-This is the waiting room?
-Yes.

868
00:54:22,280 --> 00:54:23,520
Ohh... That's fine.

869
00:54:23,680 --> 00:54:25,180
Is there really someone in there?

870
00:54:25,280 --> 00:54:28,040
Yes. This room can be locked
only from the inside...

871
00:54:28,240 --> 00:54:32,840
...so someone must be inside.
And this is the only entrance.

872
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:35,680
It would be a big problem
if she suddenly got sick.

873
00:54:38,740 --> 00:54:41,640
Hey! Hey!

874
00:54:41,640 --> 00:54:43,480
I have no choice but to ram it open.

875
00:54:43,480 --> 00:54:45,960
Okay! All of us ram it!
Yeah, Let's go!

876
00:54:45,960 --> 00:54:46,480
Yes.

877
00:54:46,480 --> 00:54:49,800
3, 2, 1... Go!

878
00:54:58,980 --> 00:55:00,800
Is she dead?

879
00:55:00,800 --> 00:55:03,280
Ran, don't look!

880
00:55:24,760 --> 00:55:31,260
Well... There's no doubt
that this may be suicide.

881
00:55:31,520 --> 00:55:34,620
This happened in a closed
room bolted from the inside.

882
00:55:34,800 --> 00:55:39,580
And if there was a person in there,
he wouldn't be able to get out...

883
00:55:40,080 --> 00:55:42,460
Suicide...

884
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:44,660
But, why would Momoka...

885
00:55:44,840 --> 00:55:48,460
The cause is the explosion
during your rehearsal.

886
00:55:49,040 --> 00:55:50,960
Explosion...?

887
00:55:51,480 --> 00:55:55,420
The explosion and Momoka's suicide...
How are they connected?

888
00:55:55,600 --> 00:55:57,320
The thing is...

889
00:55:57,480 --> 00:55:59,940
That explosion was not an accident...

890
00:56:00,120 --> 00:56:02,380
It was a case of attempted murder.

891
00:56:02,600 --> 00:56:04,380
Attempted murder?!

892
00:56:04,560 --> 00:56:05,720
What do you mean?

893
00:56:05,920 --> 00:56:07,200
Listen.

894
00:56:07,360 --> 00:56:13,760
That was a wind explosion
planned intentionally.

895
00:56:13,920 --> 00:56:15,120
"Dust" explosion.

896
00:56:15,240 --> 00:56:16,580
Director...

897
00:56:16,760 --> 00:56:19,760
Those prop swords you used
during that fight scene...

898
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:23,040
They were prepared so they
would give off sparks, right?

899
00:56:23,240 --> 00:56:27,680
Yes. They are often used in
plays to display impact.

900
00:56:27,920 --> 00:56:29,560
What about it?

901
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:34,180
The criminal knew about the contraption
in those swords which causes sparks...

902
00:56:34,400 --> 00:56:37,740
...and that ash would be flying
around during the fight.

903
00:56:37,740 --> 00:56:43,460
So, he switched the ash in the
fireplace with something flammable…

904
00:56:43,460 --> 00:56:46,800
...like potato starch, and intentionally
caused that explosion.

905
00:56:46,800 --> 00:56:50,080
Hey, that was your
deduction, wasn't it?

906
00:56:50,240 --> 00:56:53,940
Yeah. And he slipped in
a mistake here and there.

907
00:56:54,240 --> 00:56:59,120
And the person who was aiming to
take Sakuraba's life in that explosion...

908
00:56:59,320 --> 00:57:01,860
..was Momoka, who committed suicide.

909
00:57:02,160 --> 00:57:08,720
Sakuraba.You were quarrelling
with Momoka, right?

910
00:57:08,960 --> 00:57:13,600
Impossible. She caused that
explosion over a quarrel...

911
00:57:13,600 --> 00:57:16,460
And you were being threatened too?

912
00:57:17,080 --> 00:57:19,320
How would you know that?

913
00:57:19,680 --> 00:57:24,620
Well... I heard from your fellow actors...

914
00:57:24,840 --> 00:57:27,600
From inside of Momoka's belongings...

915
00:57:27,840 --> 00:57:32,280
...the magazine seemed to be used
for the threatening letter was found.

916
00:57:32,480 --> 00:57:34,520
Here. Look, here.

917
00:57:35,080 --> 00:57:38,300
Anyhow, you were
cheating on her, right?

918
00:57:38,520 --> 00:57:42,160
She's had a grudge
against you this entire time.

919
00:57:43,160 --> 00:57:45,000
That's just slander!

920
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:47,120
No matter what the motive was...

921
00:57:47,280 --> 00:57:50,880
There’s no denying that
Momoka caused that explosion.

922
00:57:51,240 --> 00:57:53,560
From her belongings...

923
00:57:53,880 --> 00:57:56,120
This was also found.

924
00:57:56,280 --> 00:57:58,120
Although, it still needs to be checked...

925
00:57:58,320 --> 00:58:02,900
But it's most likely the same
powder used in that explosion.

926
00:58:03,280 --> 00:58:05,120
Then I guess...

927
00:58:05,360 --> 00:58:07,300
The explosion was Momoka’s doing, huh...

928
00:58:07,480 --> 00:58:14,000
In other words, Momoka was trying
to kill Sakuraba in the explosion...

929
00:58:14,000 --> 00:58:18,320
but she got scared afterwards
and then committed suicide.

930
00:58:18,460 --> 00:58:20,600
Right, Kudo?

931
00:58:20,740 --> 00:58:22,600
Eh? Ah...

932
00:58:22,840 --> 00:58:28,820
Hmm, but I feel the rope she was hanging
from was too close to the entrance.

933
00:58:29,000 --> 00:58:31,000
Well, that was just by chance, wasn't it?

934
00:58:31,120 --> 00:58:34,840
My thought is that...it wasn't suicide.

935
00:58:35,040 --> 00:58:36,260
What's that?!

936
00:58:36,520 --> 00:58:38,860
It wasn't suicide?Then...

937
00:58:39,040 --> 00:58:41,600
Momoka was murdered.

938
00:58:42,400 --> 00:58:47,320
And the criminal...is most likely in here.

939
00:58:53,440 --> 00:58:58,120
That room was locked from the
inside with a bolt, right?

940
00:58:58,360 --> 00:59:00,940
If she was murdered, how
did the criminal escape?

941
00:59:01,080 --> 00:59:03,360
This isn't some manga or novel...

942
00:59:03,560 --> 00:59:05,000
I'll be solving that trick after this.

943
00:59:05,200 --> 00:59:06,800
No, there isn't any trick!

944
00:59:06,920 --> 00:59:10,440
No matter what you think about
the situation...it was suicide!

945
00:59:10,640 --> 00:59:11,380
It was murder!

946
00:59:11,480 --> 00:59:12,280
-Suicide.
-Murder!

947
00:59:12,440 --> 00:59:14,640
Suicide! Man...

948
00:59:14,640 --> 00:59:17,860
I don't know about you being a high
school detective or something...

949
00:59:17,860 --> 00:59:17,860
...but you're still an amateur.

950
00:59:18,080 --> 00:59:21,900
Hurry back home and sleep...
Hurry! Go home...

951
00:59:22,040 --> 00:59:24,680
Very well. I'll go home and sleep.

952
00:59:25,000 --> 00:59:25,840
Huh?

953
00:59:26,000 --> 00:59:28,560
Eh?! Shinichi?

954
00:59:31,060 --> 00:59:35,240
Shinichi you idiot.
Where have you gone?

955
00:59:35,400 --> 00:59:38,760
Think about how people
are looking for you...

956
00:59:38,960 --> 00:59:41,520
-Thank you very much.
-Not at all...

957
00:59:48,600 --> 00:59:50,200
What was that all about?

958
00:59:50,200 --> 00:59:51,680
What do you mean by that?

959
00:59:51,960 --> 00:59:55,580
What were you and
Fumiko talking about?

960
00:59:55,720 --> 00:59:59,660
What were we talking
about... Bookmarks.

961
00:59:59,800 --> 01:00:01,660
You're buying me one?

962
01:00:01,880 --> 01:00:03,420
Eh?! Ah, well...

963
01:00:03,600 --> 01:00:05,920
Then, I'll take this one!

964
01:00:06,080 --> 01:00:08,560
Since when did you start selling
these sakura bookmarks?

965
01:00:08,800 --> 01:00:13,440
Yes. These sakura-colored
bookmarks are only being sold...

966
01:00:13,560 --> 01:00:15,940
...for a limited time of 2
weeks until tomorrow.

967
01:00:16,080 --> 01:00:20,620
Just like with a normal bookmark,
you can affix your names on them.

968
01:00:20,760 --> 01:00:21,820
Ehh...

969
01:00:22,000 --> 01:00:25,380
These are nice, too... but
why the sakura-colored ones?

970
01:00:25,560 --> 01:00:27,380
Some reason...

971
01:00:40,940 --> 01:00:43,420
I see...

972
01:00:44,500 --> 01:00:46,560
Shinichi! What happened so suddenly?

973
01:00:46,720 --> 01:00:48,180
I know what the trick was!

974
01:00:48,180 --> 01:00:50,160
Eh? Wai, wait... Wait!

975
01:00:50,320 --> 01:00:54,400
Shinichi! Hey! What about
the bookmark!? Hey!

976
01:01:15,600 --> 01:01:18,820
The shoot will continue for now, but...

977
01:01:19,000 --> 01:01:21,700
But with that injury on your face,
you can't have the leading role.

978
01:01:21,840 --> 01:01:23,400
My condolences.

979
01:01:25,720 --> 01:01:30,180
Well... I think you were lucky not
to have died in that explosion.

980
01:01:30,400 --> 01:01:32,540
You sure are talkative, aren't you?

981
01:01:32,760 --> 01:01:34,540
Of course!

982
01:01:34,840 --> 01:01:37,180
It's your fault that Momoka is dead.

983
01:02:00,440 --> 01:02:02,700
Like I thought, that's how it was done...

984
01:02:02,700 --> 01:02:03,860
And?

985
01:02:04,000 --> 01:02:06,940
What sort of trick was it?

986
01:02:07,160 --> 01:02:13,040
The criminal first smuggled a
rope with a hoop in it. And then...

987
01:02:13,360 --> 01:02:18,600
What?! Pausing in the
middle like that is creepy!

988
01:03:04,600 --> 01:03:06,400
Shinichi!

989
01:03:22,980 --> 01:03:25,200
Dad!?

990
01:03:25,400 --> 01:03:27,940
What do you mean by raising your
hand against your own father!?

991
01:03:28,160 --> 01:03:30,080
You were refusing visitors, weren't you?

992
01:03:30,280 --> 01:03:32,900
Your trademark mustache had gotten
burnt, so you wouldn't go out in public!

993
01:03:33,040 --> 01:03:35,260
Wasn't that why you were crying, "No visitors!"?

994
01:03:35,400 --> 01:03:38,600
That’s why! But...

995
01:03:38,800 --> 01:03:42,320
This is a film studio, isn't it?

996
01:03:46,000 --> 01:03:48,160
You were looking for a mustache?!

997
01:03:48,240 --> 01:03:49,860
You must be some extra...

998
01:03:50,000 --> 01:03:52,280
You should be thankful
that you weren’t injured.

999
01:03:52,400 --> 01:03:53,900
Well, your hair was burned though.

1000
01:03:54,080 --> 01:03:55,560
Shut up!

1001
01:03:55,680 --> 01:03:58,300
They say an actor's face is their life...

1002
01:03:59,640 --> 01:04:03,060
And for me, my mustache is
more important than my life!

1003
01:04:03,580 --> 01:04:06,720
An actor's face is their life...

1004
01:04:07,160 --> 01:04:08,920
Face?

1005
01:04:11,200 --> 01:04:14,040
It's Dad's fault this will be so
much trouble to clean up.

1006
01:04:14,280 --> 01:04:16,260
Ah. No, no... Don't touch those.

1007
01:04:16,480 --> 01:04:17,580
They're scattered around so much.

1008
01:04:17,760 --> 01:04:19,580
Ah, not those... Not those either!

1009
01:04:20,480 --> 01:04:21,760
That's the one from before.

1010
01:04:21,920 --> 01:04:23,460
Eh? From before? Here, here...

1011
01:04:23,460 --> 01:04:26,640
Here and here... This might be good too.

1012
01:04:34,160 --> 01:04:37,540
Is that how it is...

1013
01:04:37,900 --> 01:04:40,940
What is it? What's the matter?

1014
01:04:41,080 --> 01:04:43,920
I understand everything now.

1015
01:04:44,560 --> 01:04:48,020
The one and only truth!

1016
01:05:03,600 --> 01:05:07,040
Heiji...Heiji!

1017
01:05:07,040 --> 01:05:09,800
No way, right? Heiji!

1018
01:05:10,840 --> 01:05:12,960
The truth is...

1019
01:05:12,960 --> 01:05:17,920
I was asked by that high school student
detective to gather all of you together.

1020
01:05:18,080 --> 01:05:20,840
Momoka's suicide was a
resolved case, right?

1021
01:05:21,040 --> 01:05:22,480
Well, about that...

1022
01:05:22,560 --> 01:05:25,180
Momoka didn't commit suicide.

1023
01:05:25,360 --> 01:05:27,940
Man, are you still saying that?

1024
01:05:28,700 --> 01:05:33,040
This was a closed room.
A murder would be impossible.

1025
01:05:33,420 --> 01:05:37,940
I will now expose the 
trick behind that.

1026
01:05:38,120 --> 01:05:43,140
First, the murderer secretly
brought in a rope with a loop...

1027
01:05:43,960 --> 01:05:47,080
Telling her that he wanted to
discuss something with her,

1028
01:05:47,360 --> 01:05:51,040
He entered the room and killed Momoka.

1029
01:05:51,460 --> 01:05:55,580
And then he tied the rope to the
beam and hung her corpse.

1030
01:05:55,880 --> 01:05:59,380
The length of the rope is the highlight of
the trick to turn this into a closed room.

1031
01:05:59,380 --> 01:06:01,480
The length of the rope?

1032
01:06:01,600 --> 01:06:03,840
It's a pendulum.

1033
01:06:04,820 --> 01:06:09,880
Though the criminal was outside of this room,
by using Momoka's body like a pendulum...

1034
01:06:09,960 --> 01:06:13,080
...he could lock the room from inside.

1035
01:06:13,240 --> 01:06:16,460
First off, the criminal 
removed the middle...

1036
01:06:16,530 --> 01:06:19,720
...clasp from the tabi 
Momoka was wearing.

1037
01:06:19,720 --> 01:06:23,920
And then they lightly fixed the
bolt to each side of her feet.

1038
01:06:24,680 --> 01:06:27,540
He then raised the 
corpse in that condition...

1039
01:06:27,610 --> 01:06:30,400
...and out through the open door.

1040
01:06:30,400 --> 01:06:34,180
When he released it, the 
corpse reacted by swinging inside.

1041
01:06:34,360 --> 01:06:37,120
Taking that opportunity to close the doors...

1042
01:06:37,360 --> 01:06:39,600
The heels of the corpse would return...

1043
01:06:39,710 --> 01:06:41,800
...and strike the door exactly 
due to the pendulum action

1044
01:06:41,800 --> 01:06:44,340
That was how they
accomplished a closed room.

1045
01:06:44,520 --> 01:06:49,220
There are a lot of marks on
both door and the bolt.

1046
01:06:49,550 --> 01:06:52,870
Most likely the criminal 
experimented many times over...

1047
01:06:52,910 --> 01:06:55,990
...in order to accomplish this trick.

1048
01:06:56,980 --> 01:06:59,680
In that case, who is the murderer?

1049
01:06:59,900 --> 01:07:01,660
The people I could think about... 

1050
01:07:01,710 --> 01:07:05,600
...were the people who bore a grudge 
against Sakuraba and Momoka.

1051
01:07:05,780 --> 01:07:09,240
The one with the highest possibility is...

1052
01:07:12,580 --> 01:07:15,560
Fumiko... You.

1053
01:07:15,940 --> 01:07:17,560
Eh?

1054
01:07:20,740 --> 01:07:22,900
Fumiko?

1055
01:07:23,040 --> 01:07:24,600
What was her motive?

1056
01:07:24,840 --> 01:07:26,260
Jealousy.

1057
01:07:26,420 --> 01:07:30,920
Fumiko was jealous of the relationship
between Sakuraba and Momoka.

1058
01:07:31,240 --> 01:07:34,980
Why... would I be jealous of those two...

1059
01:07:35,240 --> 01:07:38,960
You were Sakuraba's 
ex-lover, weren't you?

1060
01:07:39,520 --> 01:07:44,080
When I came across you two yesterday, it didn’t look like an ordinary relationship.

1061
01:07:44,080 --> 01:07:47,500
To make sure, I confirmed that with
a person from the same theatre group.

1062
01:07:47,720 --> 01:07:50,740
But Sakuraba and I had 
broke up long ago.

1063
01:07:50,920 --> 01:07:53,700
We didn't have any regrets,
so I couldn't be jealous.

1064
01:07:53,880 --> 01:07:58,740
Then why were you carrying around
that bookmark like it’s precious?

1065
01:08:00,380 --> 01:08:05,440
That's... the matchmaking peddler's
good luck bookmark, isn't it?

1066
01:08:05,840 --> 01:08:11,680
The bookmark which you received from
Sakuraba does have both of your names on it.

1067
01:08:11,920 --> 01:08:15,360
When I picked it up yesterday,
confirmed it without a doubt.

1068
01:08:16,040 --> 01:08:17,360
That was…

1069
01:08:17,600 --> 01:08:21,940
I received this from Sakuraba
when we were going out together...

1070
01:08:22,120 --> 01:08:24,480
And I just happened to be
carrying it on coincidence.

1071
01:08:24,780 --> 01:08:27,320
That would be impossible.

1072
01:08:27,480 --> 01:08:28,920
Why?

1073
01:08:29,680 --> 01:08:34,120
This sakura-colored bookmark
are limited-time goods...

1074
01:08:34,400 --> 01:08:38,800
...and were put up for
sale just 2 weeks ago.

1075
01:08:39,010 --> 01:08:43,020
You were carrying around
this bookmark like it’s precious.

1076
01:08:43,250 --> 01:08:49,580
This is the evidence that you
still had feelings for Sakuraba.

1077
01:08:54,140 --> 01:08:56,000
Fumiko...

1078
01:08:56,620 --> 01:09:02,840
Did you really attack me
and murder Momoka?

1079
01:09:04,840 --> 01:09:09,480
Sakuraba, do you still
think of me that way?

1080
01:09:09,700 --> 01:09:11,480
But...

1081
01:09:17,870 --> 01:09:18,960
Fumiko.

1082
01:09:19,220 --> 01:09:23,920
If it's difficult for you to talk here,
I'll hear your story at the station...

1083
01:09:25,710 --> 01:09:27,400
Ahh!

1084
01:09:27,880 --> 01:09:31,320
It's certainly true that I wanted
both of them to die.

1085
01:09:35,350 --> 01:09:36,270
Detective.

1086
01:09:37,310 --> 01:09:40,580
I hated Sakuraba and that woman.

1087
01:09:41,380 --> 01:09:47,320
I and Sakuraba had belonged to the
same theatre group for over 10 years.

1088
01:09:47,650 --> 01:09:51,950
And we dreamed of becoming
stars together that entire time.

1089
01:09:53,990 --> 01:09:57,650
I felt that it was natural that
I would fall in love with him.

1090
01:09:59,730 --> 01:10:03,590
But he even laid hands on that woman.

1091
01:10:04,230 --> 01:10:08,050
I was betrayed and only
he had his dream granted.

1092
01:10:08,200 --> 01:10:12,240
Having a passionate romance with a
famous Idol as a promotional stunt...

1093
01:10:12,540 --> 01:10:17,050
When that explosion occurred and
seeing Sakuraba get his face burned...

1094
01:10:17,110 --> 01:10:19,130
I honestly felt relieved.

1095
01:10:19,980 --> 01:10:21,480
Then I guess...

1096
01:10:21,630 --> 01:10:23,700
The person who killed Momoka...

1097
01:10:23,780 --> 01:10:25,040
Beats me.

1098
01:10:25,270 --> 01:10:28,290
If the police think so,
then it must be, right?

1099
01:10:29,370 --> 01:10:30,800
Fumiko...

1100
01:10:37,310 --> 01:10:41,190
Then, Sakuraba.
This time is really farewell.

1101
01:10:42,770 --> 01:10:47,300
You have no acting skill,
your face has been injured...

1102
01:10:47,430 --> 01:10:49,890
...I think that you will have
hard times from here on...

1103
01:10:50,530 --> 01:10:53,010
...but please do the best you can.

1104
01:10:59,660 --> 01:11:03,960
Ah, it’s just as I had
deduced in the end.

1105
01:11:04,260 --> 01:11:09,000
Kudo. There is always just one truth.

1106
01:11:26,640 --> 01:11:28,960
What will happen to Fumiko now?

1107
01:11:29,320 --> 01:11:32,880
Because she has voluntarily turned
 herself in as a major witness...

1108
01:11:33,040 --> 01:11:35,960
Well, a full-fledged
investigation will start now.

1109
01:11:36,140 --> 01:11:39,220
"Full-fledged investigation"?
She confessed, didn't she?

1110
01:11:39,600 --> 01:11:42,960
No physical evidence has been found yet.

1111
01:11:43,130 --> 01:11:46,660
If Fumiko left something behind at the
crime scene that would incriminate her...

1112
01:11:46,790 --> 01:11:49,170
...as the criminal, then she will
be identified as the criminal.

1113
01:11:49,710 --> 01:11:52,760
Shinichi, it's about time for our bullet train.

1114
01:11:52,990 --> 01:11:54,660
Yeah. All right.

1115
01:11:54,850 --> 01:11:56,240
You're leaving already?

1116
01:11:56,710 --> 01:11:58,750
Though I call myself a detective,
I'm still a high school student.

1117
01:11:58,800 --> 01:11:59,950
I have to go to school

1118
01:12:00,880 --> 01:12:02,480
I was responsible for the deduction.

1119
01:12:02,520 --> 01:12:04,390
The rest is police work.

1120
01:12:04,550 --> 01:12:05,310
Well then.

1121
01:12:36,660 --> 01:12:38,120
There!

1122
01:12:38,570 --> 01:12:41,320
Up there! Here!

1123
01:12:42,430 --> 01:12:45,080
Wait, Kazuha! Aren't you overdoing it?

1124
01:12:45,080 --> 01:12:48,010
It's my desire to stab the criminal!

1125
01:12:49,280 --> 01:12:50,380
There!

1126
01:12:50,840 --> 01:12:54,520
Ow, ow, ow!

1127
01:12:56,520 --> 01:12:57,680
Dad!

1128
01:12:57,780 --> 01:13:00,040
Pops, what are you doing?

1129
01:13:00,560 --> 01:13:02,390
In order to get evidence...

1130
01:13:02,460 --> 01:13:05,800
...didn’t you tell me to secretly
film using this camera?

1131
01:13:07,040 --> 01:13:08,560
Oh no!

1132
01:13:10,500 --> 01:13:11,950
Relax.

1133
01:13:14,640 --> 01:13:16,600
I struck you with the back of the sword.

1134
01:13:17,050 --> 01:13:17,650
Right?

1135
01:13:34,160 --> 01:13:35,270
Hattori!

1136
01:13:54,680 --> 01:13:56,580
Isn't it about time you gave up?

1137
01:13:57,000 --> 01:13:59,010
Playtime is over.

1138
01:14:01,290 --> 01:14:04,300
The true criminal is you.

1139
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:06,320
You.

1140
01:14:11,360 --> 01:14:13,600
Sakuraba Reiichi.

1141
01:14:20,430 --> 01:14:23,880
You...Didn't you leave?

1142
01:14:25,060 --> 01:14:27,660
If I was around, I figured
that you would think twice...

1143
01:14:27,700 --> 01:14:31,580
...about falsifying evidence,
so I put on that act.

1144
01:14:31,810 --> 01:14:33,900
This is where movies are filmed.

1145
01:14:33,960 --> 01:14:37,900
Even if we're detectives,
we can put on little acts.

1146
01:14:38,050 --> 01:14:38,850
Right, Doyle?

1147
01:14:41,200 --> 01:14:42,120
Then...

1148
01:14:43,480 --> 01:14:46,400
Making everyone suspect Fumiko...

1149
01:14:47,080 --> 01:14:48,940
Of course that was an act.

1150
01:14:49,570 --> 01:14:52,620
There was no evidence to prove
that you were the criminal...

1151
01:14:52,680 --> 01:14:55,000
...so I had to lead you to this point.

1152
01:14:55,150 --> 01:14:56,280
Sakuraba...

1153
01:14:57,190 --> 01:15:02,180
You were trying to frame Fumiko by
leaving one of her belongings...

1154
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:05,680
...at the scene of the explosion.

1155
01:15:06,100 --> 01:15:07,490
Am I wrong?

1156
01:15:07,880 --> 01:15:13,880
I was secretly tailing you with this
camera in order to get evidence.

1157
01:15:14,400 --> 01:15:15,800
Yet even so...

1158
01:15:16,670 --> 01:15:20,800
Well, with this it's clear that
Sakuraba is the true criminal...

1159
01:15:21,060 --> 01:15:23,600
But why did he cause this incident?

1160
01:15:24,030 --> 01:15:24,980
For money.

1161
01:15:25,870 --> 01:15:29,950
Sakuraba came up with the dust
explosion plot in order to get burns...

1162
01:15:30,040 --> 01:15:32,440
...he could then use to collect
a huge insurance payout.

1163
01:15:32,750 --> 01:15:35,620
Those rumors about him
insuring his face were true?

1164
01:15:35,720 --> 01:15:38,680
When I asked the police to check
with the insurance company...

1165
01:15:38,780 --> 01:15:42,740
They said that he was expected to get
an insurance payoff of 300 million yen.

1166
01:15:42,940 --> 01:15:47,060
However, his face shouldn’t have
suffered any burns in that explosion.

1167
01:15:47,270 --> 01:15:48,810
The evidence for that is...

1168
01:15:50,220 --> 01:15:53,820
This was in the costume room.

1169
01:15:54,690 --> 01:15:57,000
This is a shooting prop.
Titled "Bankoku Kohou,"

1170
01:15:57,110 --> 01:15:59,910
it's a book of international
laws from the Edo period.

1171
01:16:00,970 --> 01:16:04,090
It was a book Ryoma was
always carrying with him, right?

1172
01:16:05,140 --> 01:16:07,540
Between the pages of this book prop...

1173
01:16:09,740 --> 01:16:11,680
There was this.

1174
01:16:11,900 --> 01:16:14,890
This is a fireproof material
used in fire doors.

1175
01:16:15,640 --> 01:16:19,920
Most likely Sakuraba put this
book inside his costume...

1176
01:16:20,100 --> 01:16:24,020
Where it would protect him against
the heat and shock of the explosion.

1177
01:16:24,380 --> 01:16:27,100
Even if Sakuraba, in his role as
Ryoma, was found with this book...

1178
01:16:27,100 --> 01:16:31,440
He could say that he was role playing
and it wouldn't be unnatural, right?

1179
01:16:31,760 --> 01:16:34,160
Right. And, after the explosion...

1180
01:16:34,240 --> 01:16:36,300
...he got some charcoal or 
something from the fireplace...

1181
01:16:36,300 --> 01:16:39,960
...and used it to make a burn as
inconspicuous as possible to his own face.

1182
01:16:40,020 --> 01:16:41,580
What's that!?

1183
01:16:41,890 --> 01:16:43,100
Hey, you!

1184
01:16:43,160 --> 01:16:44,440
Show us your face!

1185
01:16:48,040 --> 01:16:52,320
Such an injury could be easily
hidden with make-up, couldn't it?!

1186
01:16:52,690 --> 01:16:54,660
Even a small injury is an injury.

1187
01:16:54,880 --> 01:16:57,000
By insisting that an actor's
face is their lives...

1188
01:16:57,270 --> 01:16:59,650
He was just trying to swindle
his way to an insurance payout.

1189
01:17:05,980 --> 01:17:08,900
It’s just as you have said it...

1190
01:17:09,060 --> 01:17:12,080
Then, Sakuraba killed Momoka?

1191
01:17:12,800 --> 01:17:16,840
Sakuraba's popularity 
rose thanks to Momoka.

1192
01:17:17,080 --> 01:17:19,980
But she immediately
became disagreeable, didn't she?

1193
01:17:20,280 --> 01:17:24,180
That Idol was both
selfish and deeply jealous.

1194
01:17:24,180 --> 01:17:27,920
And so you killed her and
made it look like a suicide.

1195
01:17:27,920 --> 01:17:30,220
Putting the magazine used to
make the threatening letter...

1196
01:17:30,290 --> 01:17:33,780
...and the bag of powder used for
the explosion in Momoka's bag...

1197
01:17:33,780 --> 01:17:36,680
You intended to frame
 the explosion on her.

1198
01:17:39,550 --> 01:17:41,670
The bookmark gift you had given Fumiko...

1199
01:17:41,730 --> 01:17:44,970
...was also a tool you used to attract
attention that you had broken up with her.

1200
01:17:45,560 --> 01:17:46,800
Anyhow...

1201
01:17:46,800 --> 01:17:49,420
By starting a new office
with the insurance money…

1202
01:17:49,800 --> 01:17:53,840
You thought that you could make
yourself a star on your own, right? Right!

1203
01:17:54,340 --> 01:17:57,380
Trifling with the hearts of two women!

1204
01:17:57,600 --> 01:17:59,470
That is absolutely unforgivable!

1205
01:17:59,700 --> 01:18:01,910
So what's wrong about it?

1206
01:18:02,680 --> 01:18:05,460
What's wrong with using women
who I didn't even like?

1207
01:18:05,700 --> 01:18:09,790
I have never loved
either Momoka or Fumiko!

1208
01:18:11,400 --> 01:18:12,480
You bastard...

1209
01:18:13,080 --> 01:18:14,980
Sakuraba!

1210
01:18:15,890 --> 01:18:19,990
Did you ever consider Fumiko's feelings...

1211
01:18:20,090 --> 01:18:21,800
...at the time when she 
confessed to the crime?

1212
01:18:21,800 --> 01:18:24,330
She could come up with...

1213
01:18:24,480 --> 01:18:27,240
...many counterarguments
to that level of deduction.

1214
01:18:28,480 --> 01:18:32,650
For example, how would it be
possible for a frail woman like her...

1215
01:18:32,720 --> 01:18:36,560
...to use her strength and raise a corpse
so it would be seen as a suicide.

1216
01:18:39,700 --> 01:18:40,770
In that case...

1217
01:18:41,310 --> 01:18:43,620
Why would Fumiko...

1218
01:18:44,090 --> 01:18:45,950
Can't you understand that?

1219
01:18:47,040 --> 01:18:50,460
Fumiko is still in love with you…

1220
01:18:50,860 --> 01:18:53,500
Despite being hurt a lot 
by your selfishness.

1221
01:18:57,630 --> 01:19:01,380
She was aware of your crime.

1222
01:19:03,120 --> 01:19:05,130
But she was never going to admit to that.

1223
01:19:06,570 --> 01:19:07,880
Even though you had broken up...

1224
01:19:07,880 --> 01:19:12,440
She's been dreaming of you
becoming a star all this time.

1225
01:19:14,720 --> 01:19:16,860
How noble!

1226
01:19:18,130 --> 01:19:20,290
For the sake of the man she loved,...

1227
01:19:20,350 --> 01:19:23,720
...she lied and made herself the criminal...

1228
01:19:23,720 --> 01:19:28,760
How would you understand the
feelings of a woman like that?

1229
01:19:37,810 --> 01:19:39,340
Fumiko...

1230
01:19:40,040 --> 01:19:41,900
For Sakuraba's sake...

1231
01:19:42,910 --> 01:19:45,180
...performed a lie as an actress.

1232
01:19:47,190 --> 01:19:49,320
But, in her final words…

1233
01:19:50,050 --> 01:19:55,680
I think that she was entrusting
her true feelings towards you.

1234
01:19:57,060 --> 01:19:58,700
Then, Sakuraba.

1235
01:19:58,970 --> 01:20:00,580
This time is really farewell.

1236
01:20:01,100 --> 01:20:03,330
Your face has been injured...

1237
01:20:03,420 --> 01:20:06,140
...and I think that you will have
hard times from here on…

1238
01:20:06,480 --> 01:20:07,960
But please do the best you can.

1239
01:20:10,370 --> 01:20:11,780
Fumiko...

1240
01:20:30,120 --> 01:20:31,130
I'm sorry.

1241
01:20:31,580 --> 01:20:34,350
For bringing you these painful emotions.

1242
01:20:38,020 --> 01:20:39,560
Sakuraba...

1243
01:20:42,420 --> 01:20:43,600
Fumiko...

1244
01:20:46,000 --> 01:20:47,360
You...

1245
01:20:59,410 --> 01:21:02,360
Forgive me for acting like that...

1246
01:21:06,590 --> 01:21:10,340
Why did you set a trap for me?

1247
01:21:13,800 --> 01:21:16,170
I believed in you...

1248
01:21:16,410 --> 01:21:18,540
...that this isn’t who you really are.

1249
01:21:37,090 --> 01:21:38,280
I...

1250
01:21:43,350 --> 01:21:45,240
Damnit…

1251
01:22:14,560 --> 01:22:16,620
I am really sorry.

1252
01:22:16,920 --> 01:22:19,520
For the sake of exposing the criminal...

1253
01:22:19,700 --> 01:22:22,030
I even asked you to perform
the role of a criminal.

1254
01:22:26,790 --> 01:22:28,320
I believed in him.

1255
01:22:29,750 --> 01:22:31,960
That he couldn't be a murderer.

1256
01:22:34,570 --> 01:22:36,660
But then I knew...

1257
01:22:37,980 --> 01:22:41,670
After you had solved the trick
of the closed room that...

1258
01:22:43,320 --> 01:22:44,960
That was in his attitude.

1259
01:22:45,100 --> 01:22:46,390
Fumiko...

1260
01:22:47,650 --> 01:22:50,530
Did you really attack me...

1261
01:22:50,620 --> 01:22:52,890
...and murder Momoka?"

1262
01:22:54,380 --> 01:22:55,980
Even if I couldn’t be there for him...

1263
01:22:57,170 --> 01:23:00,610
I at least wanted to watch
over him from a distance.

1264
01:23:02,480 --> 01:23:04,270
That’s how I feel even now.

1265
01:23:05,270 --> 01:23:07,060
Why would you go that far for him?

1266
01:23:10,240 --> 01:23:14,660
Because we are colleagues aiming
to become actors together.

1267
01:23:14,830 --> 01:23:17,570
When it comes to a beautiful
woman such as yourself...

1268
01:23:18,330 --> 01:23:21,860
You can have many more wonderful
encounters from here on.

1269
01:23:22,240 --> 01:23:24,740
This Mori Kogoro guarantees that.

1270
01:23:25,900 --> 01:23:27,150
Starting today...

1271
01:23:29,180 --> 01:23:32,320
Please start walking
towards a new tomorrow.

1272
01:23:35,130 --> 01:23:37,610
And, how about me for starters?

1273
01:23:38,740 --> 01:23:39,760
Hey, Dad!

1274
01:23:39,760 --> 01:23:40,520
Pops!

1275
01:23:41,270 --> 01:23:42,820
Eh? No...

1276
01:23:43,080 --> 01:23:45,660
That was a joke. Joke!

1277
01:23:50,410 --> 01:23:54,660
Thanks to you, Detective,
I can again start anew.

1278
01:23:56,350 --> 01:23:57,500
Thank you.

1279
01:23:57,990 --> 01:24:00,690
For finding the one and only truth.

1280
01:24:11,100 --> 01:24:12,480
"Filming Canceled"

1281
01:24:12,480 --> 01:24:15,110
Well, thanks to Doyle yelling "Escape!"...

1282
01:24:15,160 --> 01:24:18,000
...you got away from that
explosion safely, didn't you?

1283
01:24:18,070 --> 01:24:20,400
That's true. If it hadn't 
been for his voice...

1284
01:24:20,470 --> 01:24:23,380
I wouldn't have been able to protect
uncle and jump out the back.

1285
01:24:23,380 --> 01:24:28,660
But not going to see off the one who
saved your life is really messed up.

1286
01:24:28,790 --> 01:24:29,940
It's fine!

1287
01:24:33,340 --> 01:24:38,160
Anyhow, Doyle and I will
have a long relationship.

1288
01:24:39,620 --> 01:24:40,960
That Kudo guy...

1289
01:24:41,330 --> 01:24:44,400
Still pretending to be
Doyle this time around, too.

1290
01:24:47,390 --> 01:24:50,500
Next time I'll be the 
one going to Tokyo.

1291
01:24:53,710 --> 01:24:56,500
How can your father think that way?

1292
01:24:56,840 --> 01:25:00,500
"I guess I'm best suited as being
a detective and not an actor"

1293
01:25:00,500 --> 01:25:02,500
Saying that, he hurried back home.

1294
01:25:02,540 --> 01:25:04,720
When Fumiko said, "Detective"...

1295
01:25:04,790 --> 01:25:07,220
It wasn't about Dad, was it?

1296
01:25:07,280 --> 01:25:09,650
I really wonder what sort
of thought circuits he has.

1297
01:25:09,900 --> 01:25:11,080
Well, let’s go back home, too.

1298
01:25:11,130 --> 01:25:12,010
Yeah!

1299
01:25:19,930 --> 01:25:23,100
In the end, he didn't buy me one.

1300
01:25:23,960 --> 01:25:26,380
Well then, it couldn't be helped.

1301
01:25:31,160 --> 01:25:32,840
This is...?

1302
01:25:33,440 --> 01:25:35,240
I was out taking a walk this morning...

1303
01:25:35,320 --> 01:25:37,380
...I just happened find it by chance.

1304
01:25:52,210 --> 01:25:54,940
Let's hurry and get back.
We'll miss that bullet train.

1305
01:25:55,230 --> 01:25:56,290
Shinichi!

1306
01:26:00,470 --> 01:26:01,470
Thank you.

1307
01:26:04,830 --> 01:26:05,870
OK....

1308
01:26:13,320 --> 01:26:15,980
"This Drama is Fictional"

